Chapter: DeskPointerBedTest
  cites Works chapter GopUsb
  cites Works chapter GopUsbMouse
  cites Kernel chapter Hpet
  cites Foreword chapter CCE

 DOES A SCRIPTED CLICK REACH THE GUEST. This is a bed probe rather than a
 test of any app: it attaches the USB pointer exactly as `DeskVm` does,
 pumps it for a fixed span of HPET time, and prints what arrived. Run it
 under the same `-mouse-file` timeline that is meant to drive a desk, and
 the numbers say which half is at fault.

 The three readings are chosen so that each failure has its own
 signature rather than one shared silence:

   ok      -- the pointer enumerated at all. `no` means every later zero
              is explained and nothing about the timeline is in question.
   reports -- consumed HID reports. Zero with `ok yes` means the endpoint
              is bound and delivering nothing.
   moved   -- the folded position. A position that left the centre proves
              the motion bytes of those reports arrived.
   clicks  -- presses `mouse-take-click` answered. THIS IS THE ONE THE
              CAPTURES CANNOT SEE. Motion arriving with zero clicks says
              the button byte is being lost between the timeline and
              `mouse-consume`, which no screenshot of a desk can
              distinguish from a menu that ignored a hit.

 The probe prints a line per click as well as the totals, because WHEN a
 click lands relative to the timeline is what says whether a press before
 the first paint is being dropped.

Section: Body

  pb-w : Integer = 1600
  pb-h : Integer = 900

  pb-span : Integer
  pb-span = 16 * hpet-ticks-per-second

  pb-yn : Boolean -> Text
  pb-yn (v) = if v then "yes" else "no"

  pb-loop : UsbMouse, Integer, Integer -> [Console, Device.Port] Integer
  pb-loop (m) (deadline) (clicks) =
    if hpet-ticks >= deadline then act clicks end
    else act
      mv <- act mouse-pump m pb-w pb-h end
      let c = mouse-take-click m
      in if c then act
        print-line-uni ("click " & show (clicks + 1) & " at " & show (mouse-x m) & "," & show (mouse-y m) & "  buttons " & show (mouse-buttons m) & "  reports " & show (mouse-events m))
        pb-loop m deadline (clicks + 1)
      end
      else pb-loop m deadline clicks
    end

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console, Device.Port, Device.Mmio, Gpu.Compute, Gpu.Memory, Identity, Audio, Concurrent, Capability, Network.Read, Network.Write] Nothing = act
    ri <- runtime-init 0
    att <- usb-attach
    let m = att.ua-mouse
    in act
      print-line-uni ("pointer ok: " & pb-yn (m.um-ok))
      n <- pb-loop m (hpet-ticks + pb-span) 0
      print-line-uni ("clicks " & show n)
      print-line-uni ("reports " & show (mouse-events m))
      print-line-uni ("moved to " & show (mouse-x m) & "," & show (mouse-y m))
    end
  end
